 "prediction_scored": "hit: under the primary reading R1 the reproduced values are 6.95 mph for FY25 (stated 6.9) and 6.62 mph for FY26 (stated 6.5), both within the registered 0.2 mph. Secondary checks also hit: FY24 6.94 (stated 6.9) and an FY25-to-FY26 change of -0.33 mph (stated -0.4). Five of the nine readings (R1, R3, R7, R8, R9) reproduce both years; the mean of trip speeds (R2), the two looser geographies (R4, R5) and the minimal filter (R6) do not.",
 "settle": "DOT's method note for the indicator (zone set, aggregation, trip filters, holiday list and whether trip records or GPS are used) would settle the remaining 0.1 mph gap in FY26. The disagreement with mob-crz-traffic is one of measure, not of data: see notes.",
